1
00:00:32,610 --> 00:00:34,610
You’re about to face a difficult situation.

2
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:37,820
It’s a problem you didn’t cause,

3
00:00:39,570 --> 00:00:42,350
but everything will point to you.

4
00:00:44,180 --> 00:00:44,840
Me?

5
00:00:46,180 --> 00:00:47,060
Did I do something wrong?

6
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:51,980
You didn’t,

7
00:00:53,670 --> 00:00:55,840
but you’ll be accused.

8
00:00:57,180 --> 00:00:59,970
This card says the truth will be hidden,

9
00:00:59,970 --> 00:01:02,900
and the people around you will believe things that are not true.

10
00:01:03,310 --> 00:01:05,810
You’ll feel like your hands and feet are tied.

11
00:01:05,810 --> 00:01:08,800
No matter what you say, no one will listen.

12
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:10,990
How do I prevent this?

13
00:01:13,610 --> 00:01:15,039
First, don’t panic.

14
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:17,140
Second, don’t stay silent.

15
00:01:17,370 --> 00:01:19,160
If you say nothing,

16
00:01:19,160 --> 00:01:21,420
people will misunderstand you.

17
00:01:22,320 --> 00:01:23,289
And lastly,

18
00:01:24,050 --> 00:01:25,460
the person closest to you

19
00:01:26,100 --> 00:01:27,480
will be the key

20
00:01:28,550 --> 00:01:29,590
to this whole situation,

21
00:01:31,160 --> 00:01:33,960
whether they stand by your side or turn their back on you.

22
00:01:36,090 --> 00:01:36,920
Be careful.

23
00:01:37,759 --> 00:01:41,590
You’ll soon be dragged into something you didn’t cause,

24
00:01:41,970 --> 00:01:44,340
but you’ll take all the blame.

25
00:03:13,650 --> 00:03:16,340
This is unripe durian fried until crispy.

26
00:03:16,730 --> 00:03:19,820
Is this really fried durian?

27
00:03:20,490 --> 00:03:24,290
How did I live without it before?

28
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:25,110
My lord.

29
00:03:25,110 --> 00:03:25,910
Gaew!

30
00:03:25,910 --> 00:03:27,940
My lord, lord Muen went underwater.

31
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:32,650
P'Muen!

32
00:03:39,930 --> 00:03:41,270
I think you’re…

33
00:03:41,270 --> 00:03:42,200
cuter now?

34
00:03:44,780 --> 00:03:48,020
(Ayutthaya, Thai minor era 1036)

35
00:03:48,020 --> 00:03:48,710
Help!

36
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:50,290
My lord.

37
00:04:09,870 --> 00:04:10,480
Hey!

38
00:04:11,030 --> 00:04:12,610
Officer, over there!

39
00:04:12,610 --> 00:04:13,850
That way.

40
00:04:13,850 --> 00:04:14,680
After him!

41
00:04:20,850 --> 00:04:21,649
Here.

42
00:04:24,030 --> 00:04:25,270
Thank you so much.

43
00:04:25,810 --> 00:04:27,360
If it weren’t for you, I’d be in trouble.

44
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:30,740
Your accent is so good.

45
00:04:32,890 --> 00:04:34,630
I’ve lived here since I was born.

46
00:04:37,159 --> 00:04:39,590
My name is Maria Guyomar.

47
00:04:43,330 --> 00:04:45,510
And you? What's your name?

48
00:04:47,480 --> 00:04:48,440
So?

49
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:50,530
What’s your name?

50
00:04:51,310 --> 00:04:52,820
My name is... Great.

51
00:04:53,510 --> 00:04:54,130
No.

52
00:04:54,659 --> 00:04:55,570
It's Gaew.

53
00:04:56,950 --> 00:04:57,780
Gaew.

54
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:00,460
Thank you again.

55
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:06,400
Maria Guyomar.

56
00:05:07,330 --> 00:05:08,800
You can call me Mali.

57
00:05:18,100 --> 00:05:19,180
Thank you so much

58
00:05:19,820 --> 00:05:21,190
for saving my daughter.

59
00:05:21,990 --> 00:05:24,670
It’s nothing. I’m glad I could help.

60
00:05:26,510 --> 00:05:27,200
Cheers.

61
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:50,400
I made some desserts for you

62
00:05:50,710 --> 00:05:52,630
to thank you for helping me.

63
00:05:55,790 --> 00:05:56,760
So this is it.

64
00:05:59,890 --> 00:06:03,610
The name Thao Thong Kip Ma was granted by King Narai.

65
00:06:03,610 --> 00:06:06,610
And the desserts I make, Thong Yip, Thong Yod, and Foi Thong,

66
00:06:06,610 --> 00:06:09,140
all came from her recipes.

67
00:06:12,420 --> 00:06:13,350
What is it?

68
00:06:14,070 --> 00:06:14,870
It looks so good.

69
00:06:15,990 --> 00:06:16,780
Give it a try.

70
00:06:25,890 --> 00:06:26,710
Hmm.

71
00:06:28,980 --> 00:06:30,140
So skibidi.

72
00:06:31,320 --> 00:06:33,260
This is really a real Foi Thong.

73
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:37,690
This isn’t Foi Thong.

74
00:06:38,330 --> 00:06:40,490
It’s called Thong Pae.

75
00:06:42,510 --> 00:06:43,500
And…

76
00:06:44,670 --> 00:06:45,930
Ski?

77
00:06:46,420 --> 00:06:47,350
Ski what?

78
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:48,930
What does it mean?

79
00:06:49,830 --> 00:06:50,770
Skibidi.

80
00:06:51,090 --> 00:06:53,090
It means delicious.

81
00:06:53,420 --> 00:06:55,330
This tastes really amazing.

82
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:57,080
You get a like from me.

83
00:07:00,970 --> 00:07:01,690
Uh…

84
00:07:05,530 --> 00:07:07,100
It’s even better than my grandma's.

85
00:07:13,840 --> 00:07:16,540
This is Lord Muen’s sword school.

86
00:07:18,830 --> 00:07:20,580
You used to come here too.

87
00:07:46,430 --> 00:07:47,200
Whoa.

88
00:07:49,290 --> 00:07:51,860
You have a great figure.

89
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:54,400
I bet you’re rock solid.

90
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:57,650
What’s your problem, Gaew?

91
00:07:58,460 --> 00:08:00,130
Looking for trouble again?

92
00:08:03,030 --> 00:08:04,680
The way this is going…

93
00:08:05,500 --> 00:08:06,690
doesn’t look good.

94
00:08:11,050 --> 00:08:11,750
P’Yam.

95
00:08:13,050 --> 00:08:14,410
Who are they?

96
00:08:14,910 --> 00:08:16,140
They look scary.

97
00:08:17,540 --> 00:08:20,470
The one who pushed you is Muan,

98
00:08:20,470 --> 00:08:22,910
the guy who fought with you last time.

99
00:08:23,850 --> 00:08:26,190
That one is Sin.

100
00:08:26,540 --> 00:08:30,130
The one behind him is Peng.

101
00:08:31,450 --> 00:08:32,490
And…

102
00:08:33,159 --> 00:08:34,730
that one is

103
00:08:35,230 --> 00:08:36,280
Wad.

104
00:08:36,919 --> 00:08:38,650
They’re all your rivals.

105
00:08:44,520 --> 00:08:45,990
All of them?

106
00:08:46,820 --> 00:08:47,690
That’s right.

107
00:09:14,880 --> 00:09:16,140
What are you staring at?

108
00:09:22,760 --> 00:09:24,880
Are you mad I beat you at the gambling den?

109
00:09:27,050 --> 00:09:28,540
Yeah, you damn cheater.

110
00:09:40,240 --> 00:09:41,020
Muan!

111
00:09:56,530 --> 00:09:57,920
You’re always causing trouble.

112
00:10:03,890 --> 00:10:05,490
P'Muen, you should’ve asked

113
00:10:06,380 --> 00:10:08,120
before stepping in and kicking me.

114
00:10:08,780 --> 00:10:09,730
Someone like you

115
00:10:10,430 --> 00:10:12,380
doesn’t deserve it.

116
00:10:13,340 --> 00:10:14,690
All you ever do is evil.

117
00:10:15,240 --> 00:10:16,070
Evil?

118
00:10:17,740 --> 00:10:21,080
Then how about a duel with an evil guy?

119
00:10:24,780 --> 00:10:25,460
Reung!

120
00:10:25,680 --> 00:10:26,460
Stay out of this!

121
00:10:46,130 --> 00:10:49,160
If you’re still acting like a thug, and picking fights with everyone.

122
00:10:49,650 --> 00:10:51,180
Then you’re not a man.

123
00:10:51,870 --> 00:10:53,220
Just go home and wear a sinh!

124
00:10:55,880 --> 00:10:56,920
You’ve gone too far!

125
00:11:02,390 --> 00:11:03,460
A thug in a skirt?

126
00:11:08,670 --> 00:11:09,360
Yam.

127
00:11:09,830 --> 00:11:10,360
Let’s go.

128
00:11:11,090 --> 00:11:11,680
Yes, sir.

129
00:11:13,200 --> 00:11:13,750
I…

130
00:11:14,450 --> 00:11:15,490
I’m the new Gaew.

131
00:11:16,190 --> 00:11:18,140
Nice to meet you all.

132
00:11:22,390 --> 00:11:23,430
It’s nice to meet you.

133
00:11:31,710 --> 00:11:32,840
Please take care of me.

134
00:11:35,410 --> 00:11:37,240
Hello. Nice to meet you.

135
00:11:43,080 --> 00:11:44,260
Please take care of me.

136
00:11:50,890 --> 00:11:51,540
Well…

137
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:53,710
If the old Gaew

138
00:11:54,310 --> 00:11:56,040
did anything wrong to you…

139
00:11:56,620 --> 00:11:57,240
Today,

140
00:11:58,140 --> 00:11:59,410
I’m a new person now.

141
00:12:00,120 --> 00:12:01,770
I apologize for what I did in the past.

142
00:12:02,560 --> 00:12:03,650
I promise that

143
00:12:04,390 --> 00:12:05,500
from now on

144
00:12:05,980 --> 00:12:09,260
this new Gaew will be a good person.

145
00:12:09,420 --> 00:12:11,080
Let’s start over.

146
00:12:12,760 --> 00:12:16,290
I swear on my Scout’s honor.

147
00:12:16,850 --> 00:12:18,170
Yam, you should swear too.

148
00:12:18,580 --> 00:12:19,280
I swear.

149
00:12:21,220 --> 00:12:22,580
Are you trying to provoke me?

150
00:12:23,420 --> 00:12:25,800
What nonsense about this old and new Gaew?

151
00:12:26,280 --> 00:12:28,100
So the rumors that you’re different

152
00:12:29,130 --> 00:12:30,020
must be true.

153
00:12:30,550 --> 00:12:31,230
That’s right.

154
00:12:31,860 --> 00:12:34,020
I’m the new Gaew in the same body.

155
00:12:35,020 --> 00:12:35,820
You’ve lost it.

156
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:37,220
Pathetic.

157
00:12:43,340 --> 00:12:44,670
I guess even if I’m a new Gaew,

158
00:12:44,980 --> 00:12:46,330
it changes nothing.

159
00:12:49,400 --> 00:12:50,060
Good.

160
00:12:51,190 --> 00:12:53,490
Last time, you crossed me and my little brother.

161
00:12:54,220 --> 00:12:54,840
Now,

162
00:12:55,540 --> 00:12:56,820
It’s my turn to get even.

163
00:12:58,940 --> 00:12:59,890
Stop right there!

164
00:13:05,250 --> 00:13:07,080
Dech, why are you stopping me?

165
00:13:07,740 --> 00:13:09,020
Don’t you remember what he did to me?

166
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:12,380
Why keep holding onto the grudge?

167
00:13:13,540 --> 00:13:16,770
Did you forget how Gaew looked down on us?

168
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:19,170
So why the change of heart today?

169
00:13:21,420 --> 00:13:23,020
Sin, Gaew.

170
00:13:23,970 --> 00:13:26,060
You two still have unfinished business, right?

171
00:13:26,380 --> 00:13:27,010
-Yes.
-No.

172
00:13:30,250 --> 00:13:30,840
Good.

173
00:13:31,140 --> 00:13:33,320
Since you want to settle this.

174
00:13:34,070 --> 00:13:36,520
Dech and I will be your witnesses.

175
00:13:36,710 --> 00:13:37,380
Hey.

176
00:13:45,920 --> 00:13:47,390
Settle what?

177
00:13:49,790 --> 00:13:50,420
Gaew.

178
00:14:15,300 --> 00:14:16,280
Sin, don’t!

179
00:14:20,470 --> 00:14:21,180
Reung.

180
00:14:21,490 --> 00:14:22,230
Reung!

181
00:14:23,420 --> 00:14:24,140
Reung!

182
00:14:24,450 --> 00:14:25,140
Rich!

183
00:14:42,050 --> 00:14:42,700
Rich.

184
00:14:48,230 --> 00:14:48,840
Reung.

185
00:14:50,310 --> 00:14:51,180
I’m sorry.

186
00:14:51,570 --> 00:14:53,800
You got hurt because of me.

187
00:14:56,570 --> 00:14:58,530
Now’s not the time to apologize.

188
00:14:59,520 --> 00:15:01,020
Let Wad treat his wound first.

189
00:15:03,420 --> 00:15:04,040
Wad.

190
00:15:11,520 --> 00:15:13,270
A sword wound needs medicine right away.

191
00:15:15,350 --> 00:15:16,170
Hold on, Wad.

192
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:19,520
The bleeding hasn’t stopped.

193
00:15:19,770 --> 00:15:20,780
You need to stop it first.

194
00:15:21,920 --> 00:15:23,000
I know.

195
00:15:23,370 --> 00:15:25,510
That’s what I’m going to do.

196
00:15:25,970 --> 00:15:27,470
Why are you stopping me?

197
00:15:28,960 --> 00:15:30,760
Medicine that stops the bleeding?

198
00:15:37,330 --> 00:15:38,590
You mean Siam weed powder?

199
00:15:39,250 --> 00:15:40,820
No, not Siam weed powder.

200
00:15:41,630 --> 00:15:42,480
It’s even better.

201
00:15:48,450 --> 00:15:49,620
Oh.

202
00:15:50,480 --> 00:15:51,370
Tienchi Ginseng.

203
00:15:55,720 --> 00:15:57,820
Do you know what this is?

204
00:15:58,610 --> 00:16:00,610
It’s a Chinese herbal root,

205
00:16:00,610 --> 00:16:03,490
which helps stop bleeding and prevents blood clots.

206
00:16:05,310 --> 00:16:07,430
You probably don’t know better than me.

207
00:16:07,920 --> 00:16:09,900
I’m Muen Royal Pharmacist, after all.

208
00:16:10,410 --> 00:16:12,110
What a bluff.

209
00:16:12,900 --> 00:16:14,810
Muen Royal Pharmacist.

210
00:16:15,760 --> 00:16:17,990
Thong Ek: The Herbal Master.

211
00:16:21,430 --> 00:16:22,020
Bluff?

212
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:25,540
Thong Ek?

213
00:16:25,940 --> 00:16:26,770
What’s that?

214
00:16:28,600 --> 00:16:29,500
I’m not telling you.

215
00:16:43,290 --> 00:16:44,120
Reung.

216
00:16:45,740 --> 00:16:46,850
I’ll take you home.

217
00:16:47,940 --> 00:16:49,110
It’s okay, Gaew.

218
00:16:50,790 --> 00:16:51,960
I’ll take him home.

219
00:16:53,100 --> 00:16:53,870
Come on, Reung.

220
00:16:55,710 --> 00:16:56,500
Slowly.

221
00:17:04,910 --> 00:17:05,829
Alright, P’ Muen.

222
00:17:06,480 --> 00:17:07,210
Let’s go home.

223
00:17:12,180 --> 00:17:12,869
P’ Muen?

224
00:17:16,170 --> 00:17:17,140
What’s wrong?

225
00:17:17,819 --> 00:17:19,380
Why don’t you talk to me?

226
00:17:24,640 --> 00:17:26,730
Oh.

227
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:29,660
Are you upset

228
00:17:30,040 --> 00:17:33,120
because I haven’t thanked you for saving me?

229
00:17:36,400 --> 00:17:39,460
The one who helped you was Reung.

230
00:17:40,630 --> 00:17:41,460
Not me.

231
00:17:45,710 --> 00:17:46,580
That’s true.

232
00:17:47,960 --> 00:17:49,380
If it weren’t for Reung.

233
00:17:50,380 --> 00:17:51,720
I’d surely be dead.

234
00:17:53,620 --> 00:17:54,720
Seriously.

235
00:17:55,700 --> 00:17:57,040
He’s handsome,

236
00:17:58,020 --> 00:17:59,380
cool,

237
00:18:00,540 --> 00:18:01,920
and perfect.

238
00:18:08,160 --> 00:18:09,320
Why did you push me?

239
00:18:09,740 --> 00:18:10,740
What’s your problem?

240
00:18:12,450 --> 00:18:13,920
You’re annoying.

241
00:18:17,170 --> 00:18:18,150
What’s wrong with you?

242
00:18:18,820 --> 00:18:21,680
I was just talking about how Reung saved my life.

243
00:18:22,710 --> 00:18:23,220
Well,

244
00:18:25,260 --> 00:18:26,410
it bothers me.

245
00:18:27,230 --> 00:18:28,150
Everything you do.

246
00:18:28,610 --> 00:18:30,760
The way you went out without telling me.

247
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:34,350
The way you act like you’re a doctor.

248
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:36,330
And the way you looked so worried,

249
00:18:36,330 --> 00:18:38,810
as if Reung was about to die.

250
00:18:40,720 --> 00:18:41,480
From now on,

251
00:18:42,200 --> 00:18:44,920
I’ll watch your every move.

252
00:18:47,270 --> 00:18:48,810
Why are you latching out at me?

253
00:18:50,390 --> 00:18:51,220
Let’s go home.

254
00:18:55,450 --> 00:18:56,550
I said, go home!

255
00:19:01,420 --> 00:19:02,890
Yam, let’s go.

256
00:19:03,400 --> 00:19:04,040
Yes, sir.

257
00:19:17,050 --> 00:19:18,500
What’s this feeling?

258
00:19:20,550 --> 00:19:21,780
What kind of feeling?

259
00:19:24,510 --> 00:19:25,280
Go home!

260
00:20:11,260 --> 00:20:11,910
Yam.

261
00:20:12,280 --> 00:20:12,840
Yes.

262
00:20:13,250 --> 00:20:14,000
Come on.

263
00:20:14,540 --> 00:20:17,160
I don’t want to stay here and annoy anyone.

264
00:20:24,760 --> 00:20:25,600
My lord.

265
00:20:32,840 --> 00:20:33,560
My lord.

266
00:20:33,560 --> 00:20:35,150
Follow me, Yam.

267
00:20:39,220 --> 00:20:39,970
Dech.

268
00:20:39,970 --> 00:20:40,510
Huh?

269
00:20:41,710 --> 00:20:42,880
What are you looking at?

270
00:20:43,940 --> 00:20:45,030
Nothing.

271
00:20:46,120 --> 00:20:47,850
I was just thinking about work.

272
00:20:49,720 --> 00:20:50,740
Work?

273
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:54,810
I'll get going.

274
00:20:56,320 --> 00:20:57,750
Let’s go, Pin.

275
00:21:07,980 --> 00:21:13,980
(What is that mark upon your rosy cheeks?)

276
00:21:16,500 --> 00:21:19,620
(Did some insect dare to kiss you in your sleep?)

277
00:21:21,440 --> 00:21:22,420
Who wrote this poem?

278
00:21:32,380 --> 00:21:35,580
What is that mark upon your rosy cheeks?

279
00:21:36,150 --> 00:21:39,030
Did some insect dare to kiss you in your sleep?

280
00:22:39,160 --> 00:22:40,110
What is this?

281
00:22:40,980 --> 00:22:42,190
Whoa.

282
00:22:48,050 --> 00:22:49,010
My lord.

283
00:22:49,410 --> 00:22:51,930
Why are we secretly following Lord Gaew?

284
00:22:54,810 --> 00:22:56,730
I’m afraid he’s going to cause trouble,

285
00:22:57,840 --> 00:22:59,410
so I can’t let him out of my sight.

286
00:23:00,170 --> 00:23:03,620
Then why didn’t we take the same boat as him?

287
00:23:03,900 --> 00:23:04,860
Hey, Pin.

288
00:23:05,620 --> 00:23:06,940
Why so many questions?

289
00:23:08,640 --> 00:23:11,470
If I don't ask, don’t say anything.

290
00:23:12,520 --> 00:23:13,230
Yes, my lord.

291
00:23:56,600 --> 00:23:57,520
Hurry, follow him.

292
00:24:03,510 --> 00:24:04,270
Come here!

293
00:24:04,610 --> 00:24:06,980
Let me go! Let me go!

294
00:24:06,980 --> 00:24:08,660
Help me!

295
00:24:08,860 --> 00:24:09,530
Hey!

296
00:24:09,820 --> 00:24:11,850
Help!

297
00:24:40,060 --> 00:24:40,990
Don’t!

298
00:24:50,640 --> 00:24:51,940
Lord Luang Surasakorn?

299
00:24:52,430 --> 00:24:53,760
You filthy scum!

300
00:24:54,330 --> 00:24:57,700
I’ll have all of you arrested.

301
00:24:58,720 --> 00:24:59,470
Run!

302
00:25:06,150 --> 00:25:07,390
Are you alright?

303
00:25:10,090 --> 00:25:11,440
I’m fine.

304
00:25:12,270 --> 00:25:12,970
Gaew.

305
00:25:13,860 --> 00:25:15,010
What trouble is it this time?

306
00:25:15,530 --> 00:25:16,860
Think whatever you want.

307
00:25:24,900 --> 00:25:26,530
Lord Muen Sunthorn Thewa.

308
00:25:27,600 --> 00:25:29,480
Do you know this brave man?

309
00:25:31,070 --> 00:25:32,340
Brave?

310
00:25:36,420 --> 00:25:37,830
He’s my relative.

311
00:25:38,350 --> 00:25:39,260
His name is Gaew.

312
00:25:41,400 --> 00:25:42,180
Gaew.

313
00:25:45,440 --> 00:25:46,910
Thank you so much.

314
00:25:47,490 --> 00:25:49,290
You’ve saved me twice now.

315
00:25:52,280 --> 00:25:55,280
If this gentleman hadn’t helped me,

316
00:25:55,730 --> 00:25:56,900
I wouldn’t have made it.

317
00:25:58,050 --> 00:25:59,790
Gaew, remove your hand.

318
00:26:01,130 --> 00:26:02,250
I said remove it.

319
00:26:03,020 --> 00:26:03,750
Come here.

320
00:26:08,410 --> 00:26:09,660
Please forgive him, my lord.

321
00:26:10,720 --> 00:26:12,980
Gaew didn’t know any better,

322
00:26:13,660 --> 00:26:15,140
and overstepped his bounds.

323
00:26:15,530 --> 00:26:16,370
It’s alright.

324
00:26:17,280 --> 00:26:18,710
Lord Muen Sunthorn Thewa.

325
00:26:19,250 --> 00:26:20,030
I don’t mind.

326
00:26:21,080 --> 00:26:24,540
Thank you so much, Lord Luang Surasakorn.

327
00:26:25,240 --> 00:26:26,960
If it weren’t for your protection,

328
00:26:28,310 --> 00:26:30,410
my shop would’ve suffered immeasurable damage.

329
00:26:38,310 --> 00:26:39,110
From now on,

330
00:26:39,800 --> 00:26:41,610
I won’t let anyone

331
00:26:42,270 --> 00:26:44,040
dare treat you like that again.

332
00:26:45,040 --> 00:26:45,890
I promise.

333
00:26:51,710 --> 00:26:54,300
What should I call you?

334
00:26:56,090 --> 00:26:58,760
Maria Guyomar.

335
00:27:01,930 --> 00:27:04,700
Thank you once again.

336
00:27:06,650 --> 00:27:08,840
You can call me Falcon.

337
00:27:14,410 --> 00:27:15,130
Alright.

338
00:27:17,350 --> 00:27:20,010
Maria Guyomar.

339
00:27:21,780 --> 00:27:22,970
Falcon.

340
00:27:25,450 --> 00:27:26,460
So…

341
00:27:27,310 --> 00:27:28,830
this is it.

342
00:27:30,080 --> 00:27:31,620
Love Destiny.

343
00:27:35,620 --> 00:27:36,810
Love Destiny?

344
00:27:38,650 --> 00:27:40,240
Is that what you said?

345
00:27:40,870 --> 00:27:41,620
Yes.

346
00:27:45,890 --> 00:27:47,240
You can speak English?

347
00:27:48,290 --> 00:27:49,350
Yes, I can.

348
00:27:50,530 --> 00:27:52,300
I’m pleased to make your acquaintance.

349
00:27:54,260 --> 00:27:55,090
Nice.

350
00:27:55,090 --> 00:27:55,830
Come.

351
00:27:56,530 --> 00:27:59,270
Let us drink to celebrate this occasion.

352
00:28:00,510 --> 00:28:01,690
My pleasure.

353
00:28:15,000 --> 00:28:15,870
Yam.

354
00:28:19,090 --> 00:28:19,890
Yam.

355
00:28:21,090 --> 00:28:23,600
Your master got into trouble at the market.

356
00:28:24,730 --> 00:28:26,900
Why weren’t you looking after him?

357
00:28:27,090 --> 00:28:28,790
I wanted to follow him,

358
00:28:28,790 --> 00:28:30,550
but he ordered me not to.

359
00:28:30,810 --> 00:28:33,160
How could I disobey his orders?

360
00:28:39,660 --> 00:28:41,370
You could secretly follow him.

361
00:28:41,900 --> 00:28:44,170
What an idiot. You couldn’t even think of that.

362
00:28:44,250 --> 00:28:45,160
What about you?

363
00:28:45,510 --> 00:28:47,980
Why aren’t you with Lord Muen? Why are you here?

364
00:28:49,630 --> 00:28:51,520
He told me to go back.

365
00:28:51,890 --> 00:28:53,560
How could I say no?

366
00:28:53,560 --> 00:28:55,700
See? You’re just like me.

367
00:28:55,700 --> 00:28:58,060
We have to obey our masters, idiot.

368
00:28:58,500 --> 00:28:59,480
You’re the fool.

369
00:28:59,850 --> 00:29:01,500
I’d rather be a fool than an idiot.

370
00:29:06,040 --> 00:29:09,120
Don’t you know which one’s worse?

371
00:29:09,120 --> 00:29:09,900
So foolish.

372
00:29:09,900 --> 00:29:10,920
Where are you going?

373
00:29:10,920 --> 00:29:12,690
I’m going fishing, you idiot!

374
00:29:13,510 --> 00:29:14,630
You fool!

375
00:29:18,370 --> 00:29:19,180
Tonight,

376
00:29:20,170 --> 00:29:21,780
drinks are on me.

377
00:29:22,250 --> 00:29:24,150
Please help yourselves.

378
00:29:24,480 --> 00:29:26,870
Yeah!

379
00:29:28,980 --> 00:29:29,970
Cheers.

380
00:29:43,410 --> 00:29:45,000
Maybe not.

381
00:29:46,750 --> 00:29:48,010
What do you mean, maybe not?

382
00:29:50,700 --> 00:29:51,860
Maybe not for me.

383
00:29:56,530 --> 00:29:57,800
Come on, Gaew.

384
00:29:59,520 --> 00:30:00,310
Well…

385
00:30:00,590 --> 00:30:01,470
I…

386
00:30:14,700 --> 00:30:15,660
Very good.

387
00:30:19,810 --> 00:30:20,660
Dech.

388
00:30:22,020 --> 00:30:22,780
It’s alright.

389
00:30:23,190 --> 00:30:23,930
Gaew.

390
00:30:24,370 --> 00:30:25,700
Um, I…

391
00:30:29,870 --> 00:30:30,820
Gaew.

392
00:30:41,330 --> 00:30:42,120
Come on.

393
00:30:42,540 --> 00:30:44,430
Let me pour you another drink.

394
00:30:44,920 --> 00:30:45,910
Thank you.

395
00:31:08,950 --> 00:31:11,290
How much does your smile cost, Boss?

396
00:31:13,180 --> 00:31:16,000
The day you love me will be the day I close the job.

397
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:18,390
Shall we get started? Stopping it only makes it more hot.

398
00:31:18,390 --> 00:31:21,000
Hot, hot, hot.

399
00:32:01,640 --> 00:32:02,620
Gaew!

400
00:32:03,630 --> 00:32:04,480
Gaew?

401
00:32:08,230 --> 00:32:08,950
Gaew.

402
00:32:12,030 --> 00:32:13,200
I’m sorry.

403
00:32:14,040 --> 00:32:16,160
I should head home now.

404
00:32:19,230 --> 00:32:21,190
Everyone, enjoy yourselves.

405
00:32:22,420 --> 00:32:23,420
I’ll walk Maria home.

406
00:32:24,700 --> 00:32:27,150
It’s alright, I can go by myself.

407
00:32:27,950 --> 00:32:31,300
I told you I’d take good care of you.

408
00:32:34,130 --> 00:32:35,260
Please let me walk you home.

409
00:32:40,380 --> 00:32:41,270
Alright.

410
00:32:53,210 --> 00:32:57,990
Stop acting all cool as if you have a crown!

411
00:32:57,990 --> 00:32:58,960
That’s enough, Gaew.

412
00:32:58,960 --> 00:33:05,260
Deep down you adore me. You obviously care!

413
00:33:05,260 --> 00:33:06,380
Let’s go home, Gaew.

414
00:33:06,380 --> 00:33:08,370
It’s no big deal. Don’t make a fuss.

415
00:33:08,370 --> 00:33:09,280
Enough. Get up.

416
00:33:09,280 --> 00:33:11,590
If I’m adorable, then adore me.

417
00:33:12,100 --> 00:33:13,630
You love me.

418
00:33:13,630 --> 00:33:14,600
That’s enough.

419
00:33:14,600 --> 00:33:16,420
You’re just pretending you don’t.

420
00:33:16,600 --> 00:33:22,060
Stop acting all cool as if you have a crown.

421
00:33:22,060 --> 00:33:29,440
Deep down you adore me. You obviously care.

422
00:33:46,810 --> 00:33:49,860
How long have you been living in Ayutthaya?

423
00:33:51,300 --> 00:33:52,560
I was born here.

424
00:33:53,170 --> 00:33:55,990
My father loved this city because the people are kind.

425
00:33:57,540 --> 00:33:59,620
But it’s not that safe.

426
00:34:00,860 --> 00:34:02,500
That’s just how big cities

427
00:34:03,120 --> 00:34:04,390
and capital cities are.

428
00:34:05,410 --> 00:34:06,940
If anything bothers you,

429
00:34:07,400 --> 00:34:08,420
you can tell me.

430
00:34:09,389 --> 00:34:10,360
I’ll help you

431
00:34:12,570 --> 00:34:13,699
as much as I can.

432
00:34:27,520 --> 00:34:29,290
I’ll get going now.

433
00:34:53,650 --> 00:34:54,690
Who are you?

434
00:35:33,120 --> 00:35:34,290
Who’s behind this?

435
00:35:39,940 --> 00:35:40,860
Falcon!

436
00:35:44,050 --> 00:35:45,430
Get back inside.

437
00:36:41,300 --> 00:36:41,990
Hey.

438
00:36:42,190 --> 00:36:43,470
Wait, Gaew!

439
00:36:43,760 --> 00:36:44,440
Gaew!

440
00:36:45,100 --> 00:36:47,000
Here, use this.

441
00:36:58,960 --> 00:37:00,020
A chamber pot!

442
00:37:02,800 --> 00:37:04,220
Why do you hate me so much?

443
00:37:17,520 --> 00:37:18,940
Sleep properly.

444
00:38:39,660 --> 00:38:40,800
P’ Muen.

445
00:38:41,560 --> 00:38:44,140
Why do you hate me so much?

446
00:38:45,930 --> 00:38:49,090
Am I really that annoying?

447
00:39:15,110 --> 00:39:16,560
What’s happening to me?

448
00:39:17,940 --> 00:39:21,520
Why is my heart racing like this?

449
00:40:25,930 --> 00:40:26,890
My lord.

450
00:40:33,590 --> 00:40:34,850
How are you feeling?

451
00:40:36,980 --> 00:40:38,660
I drank too much last night.

452
00:40:39,570 --> 00:40:41,350
I don’t even remember how I came back.

453
00:40:42,180 --> 00:40:44,700
Lord Muen carried you all the way here,

454
00:40:44,700 --> 00:40:48,090
wiping you down and taking care of you.

455
00:41:22,030 --> 00:41:25,230
Thank you for taking care of me all night.

456
00:41:25,230 --> 00:41:26,260
It’s not alright.

457
00:41:26,260 --> 00:41:27,200
P’ Muen…

458
00:41:27,860 --> 00:41:28,880
I…

459
00:41:29,420 --> 00:41:30,330
Gaew.

460
00:41:37,030 --> 00:41:37,960
Gaew.

461
00:41:38,400 --> 00:41:39,010
Oh.

462
00:41:42,660 --> 00:41:44,080
When did you get here?

463
00:41:44,850 --> 00:41:46,270
I thought you were in your room.

464
00:41:47,230 --> 00:41:48,290
What are you doing?

465
00:41:49,340 --> 00:41:50,820
You’ve been talking to yourself.

466
00:41:51,850 --> 00:41:53,840
I was practicing how to thank you.

467
00:41:55,910 --> 00:41:58,000
You mean last night?

468
00:42:01,820 --> 00:42:03,820
For carrying you back to your room?

469
00:42:05,220 --> 00:42:06,160
I didn’t do that.

470
00:42:09,270 --> 00:42:10,700
I haven’t said that…

471
00:42:11,320 --> 00:42:13,540
it’s you who carried me.

472
00:42:17,070 --> 00:42:18,450
You’re acting cool again.

473
00:42:20,540 --> 00:42:21,690
I want to tell you something.

474
00:42:24,200 --> 00:42:25,950
It's about Mali.

475
00:42:27,440 --> 00:42:28,660
Maria Guyomar?

476
00:42:30,280 --> 00:42:31,800
Hm, Mali?

477
00:42:32,590 --> 00:42:33,420
Yes.

478
00:42:33,970 --> 00:42:35,730
The fabric shop owner

479
00:42:36,400 --> 00:42:38,290
who was with Lord Luang Surasakorn.

480
00:42:38,290 --> 00:42:40,100
I know him.

481
00:42:45,860 --> 00:42:46,720
P’Muen,

482
00:42:53,820 --> 00:42:55,000
I know that

483
00:42:56,740 --> 00:42:57,970
those two

484
00:42:58,780 --> 00:42:59,880
will be dating soon.

485
00:43:00,790 --> 00:43:01,390
Huh?

486
00:43:02,690 --> 00:43:03,680
What’s dating?

487
00:43:06,710 --> 00:43:08,480
It means…

488
00:43:08,790 --> 00:43:09,850
this.

489
00:43:11,600 --> 00:43:12,380
Oh.

490
00:43:12,850 --> 00:43:13,750
A couple.

491
00:43:16,500 --> 00:43:17,840
And I also know

492
00:43:18,680 --> 00:43:19,980
that the two of them

493
00:43:20,500 --> 00:43:21,660
are going to get married.

494
00:43:24,230 --> 00:43:25,970
How do you know that?

495
00:43:27,040 --> 00:43:28,500
I just do.

496
00:43:30,950 --> 00:43:31,850
That’s ridiculous.

497
00:43:33,210 --> 00:43:34,700
They follow different denominations.

498
00:43:34,980 --> 00:43:36,260
How can they get married?

499
00:43:36,550 --> 00:43:37,870
I’m serious.

500
00:43:38,740 --> 00:43:39,720
I know.

501
00:43:40,900 --> 00:43:41,770
Fine.

502
00:43:41,770 --> 00:43:43,500
I won’t argue with you.

503
00:43:46,100 --> 00:43:48,000
But what I’m curious about is

504
00:43:49,940 --> 00:43:52,000
how could you speak a foreign language?

505
00:43:54,150 --> 00:43:56,380
Lord Muen, we’ve got trouble!

506
00:43:58,150 --> 00:44:00,740
Muen Reung Ratchaphakdi has arrived with the police.

507
00:44:05,170 --> 00:44:06,660
Oh my, Muen Reung!

508
00:44:08,200 --> 00:44:09,420
Why are you arresting me?

509
00:44:11,180 --> 00:44:13,010
What happened, Muen Reung?

510
00:44:13,900 --> 00:44:16,600
Gaew is the prime suspect in a murder case.

511
00:44:16,600 --> 00:44:18,030
Murder?

512
00:44:18,580 --> 00:44:20,180
Me? A murderer?

513
00:44:22,360 --> 00:44:23,550
Calm down, Reung.

514
00:44:24,140 --> 00:44:26,120
This must be a misunderstanding.

515
00:44:26,850 --> 00:44:28,820
I hope so too, Dech.

516
00:44:29,370 --> 00:44:32,580
But my master, Khun Ratchapinit,

517
00:44:32,580 --> 00:44:36,260
received information that Gaew did it,

518
00:44:40,380 --> 00:44:43,160
so we have to take him in for questioning.

519
00:44:44,350 --> 00:44:45,100
Take him away.

520
00:44:46,260 --> 00:44:47,030
My lord.

521
00:44:47,590 --> 00:44:48,330
My lord!

522
00:44:48,650 --> 00:44:49,650
Why are you arresting me?

523
00:44:49,650 --> 00:44:51,840
Let me go! I didn’t kill anyone!

524
00:44:52,220 --> 00:44:53,580
I’ve never killed anyone!

525
00:44:54,000 --> 00:44:54,860
Please excuse us.

526
00:44:58,440 --> 00:44:59,580
I’ll follow them.

527
00:45:07,820 --> 00:45:10,110
P’ Muen, help me!

528
00:45:11,800 --> 00:45:12,830
I didn’t do it.

529
00:45:13,490 --> 00:45:15,160
I didn’t kill anyone.

530
00:45:28,950 --> 00:45:30,080
What happened?

531
00:45:30,710 --> 00:45:32,580
There was a murder last night.

532
00:45:33,980 --> 00:45:35,700
The prime suspect is

533
00:45:36,640 --> 00:45:37,410
Gaew.

534
00:45:42,950 --> 00:45:44,950
Who was the victim?

535
00:45:45,700 --> 00:45:46,470
Dam.

536
00:45:46,830 --> 00:45:48,220
A poet at the pier.

537
00:45:48,690 --> 00:45:50,500
His body was found at the back of the market.

538
00:46:18,670 --> 00:46:19,540
Falcon!

539
00:46:20,180 --> 00:46:21,670
Falcon, please help me!

540
00:46:21,670 --> 00:46:22,480
Falcon!

541
00:46:24,130 --> 00:46:24,910
Falcon.

542
00:46:28,790 --> 00:46:31,150
I swear I didn’t kill him last night.

543
00:46:31,390 --> 00:46:32,440
I didn’t kill him.

544
00:46:32,440 --> 00:46:34,450
Please testify that I’m innocent.

545
00:46:34,940 --> 00:46:35,690
Please.

546
00:46:36,060 --> 00:46:36,790
Falcon.

547
00:46:37,160 --> 00:46:37,800
Please.

548
00:46:38,040 --> 00:46:40,040
You can speak a foreign language?

549
00:47:18,650 --> 00:47:21,290
If you don’t confess, we’ll whip you until you do!

550
00:47:21,290 --> 00:47:24,060
I’m sorry I couldn’t help you.

551
00:47:24,420 --> 00:47:27,620
Just treating my wounds is more than enough.

552
00:47:27,940 --> 00:47:31,200
Why do I keep looking at you,

553
00:47:31,430 --> 00:47:34,040
whether you’re asleep or awake?

554
00:47:34,660 --> 00:47:38,070
I hereby appoint you as Phra Sriprach.

555
00:47:38,070 --> 00:47:41,550
If I wish to admire the lotus in your hand,

556
00:47:41,550 --> 00:47:44,140
would you allow me?

557
00:47:53,040 --> 00:47:54,320
Let me take a quick nap.

558
00:47:58,180 --> 00:48:00,230
Hello, food delivery is here.

559
00:48:01,170 --> 00:48:02,060
Did you order it?

560
00:48:02,560 --> 00:48:04,690
-Did you?
-No.

561
00:48:04,690 --> 00:48:05,820
I didn’t order anything.

562
00:48:05,820 --> 00:48:06,860
Neither did I.

563
00:48:06,860 --> 00:48:07,460
What?

564
00:48:07,720 --> 00:48:09,170
Who ordered the food?

565
00:48:10,400 --> 00:48:11,700
I did.

566
00:48:11,990 --> 00:48:13,030
I ordered fried chicken.

567
00:48:13,030 --> 00:48:13,530
Huh?

568
00:48:13,530 --> 00:48:15,460
That’ll be 320 baht.

569
00:48:15,460 --> 00:48:16,490
Can I scan the QR code?

570
00:48:16,490 --> 00:48:17,600
Sure.

571
00:48:17,890 --> 00:48:18,830
Enjoy your meal.

572
00:48:18,830 --> 00:48:20,100
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

573
00:48:22,600 --> 00:48:24,150
Fried chicken?

574
00:48:24,530 --> 00:48:25,310
Yes.

575
00:48:25,860 --> 00:48:26,740
Why?

576
00:48:39,390 --> 00:48:40,510
Get ready.

577
00:48:41,200 --> 00:48:41,960
Five.

578
00:48:42,320 --> 00:48:42,980
Four.

579
00:48:43,540 --> 00:48:44,390
Three.

580
00:48:45,080 --> 00:48:45,880
Two.

581
00:48:46,320 --> 00:48:47,030
One.

582
00:48:47,660 --> 00:48:50,740
Right this way.

583
00:48:51,100 --> 00:48:52,050
Come on in!

584
00:48:55,510 --> 00:48:57,340
A bridge collapsed onto the car.

585
00:49:01,250 --> 00:49:02,250
Seriously.

586
00:49:11,170 --> 00:49:12,650
I thought you’d already gone home.

587
00:49:22,670 --> 00:49:24,850
I’m sorry about last night.

588
00:49:26,330 --> 00:49:27,030
Mhm.

589
00:49:30,780 --> 00:49:32,490
Can I make it up to you with a coffee?

590
00:49:53,440 --> 00:49:55,050
Don’t do it again, kiddo.

591
00:49:57,660 --> 00:49:59,160
I’m not a kid.

592
00:50:01,960 --> 00:50:02,810
Then, little boy.

593
00:50:04,600 --> 00:50:05,730
You called me a boy.

594
00:50:06,500 --> 00:50:08,620
Then what am I supposed to call you?

595
00:50:08,620 --> 00:50:09,380
Brother.

596
00:50:09,680 --> 00:50:11,430
Just call me Brother.

597
00:50:18,390 --> 00:50:19,870
Then I’ll call you…

598
00:50:20,890 --> 00:50:21,660
Big bro.

599
00:50:24,280 --> 00:50:25,120
Big bro?

600
00:50:27,580 --> 00:50:28,640
Very good.

601
00:51:01,490 --> 00:51:03,320
You did a great job today, kiddo.

602
00:51:03,910 --> 00:51:05,580
You were amazing too, Big Bro.

603
00:51:06,150 --> 00:51:07,740
When you put it in,

604
00:51:08,210 --> 00:51:09,370
I was so nervous.

605
00:51:10,570 --> 00:51:11,940
The breathing tube?

606
00:51:12,220 --> 00:51:12,930
Yeah.

607
00:51:17,700 --> 00:51:19,270
So how are you getting home?

608
00:51:20,130 --> 00:51:21,680
By bus.

609
00:51:22,690 --> 00:51:23,580
The bus?

610
00:51:23,940 --> 00:51:26,390
Want a ride with me? We’re both off today.

611
00:51:28,440 --> 00:51:29,330
Really?

612
00:51:30,790 --> 00:51:31,760
Of course.

613
00:51:35,070 --> 00:51:36,100
Do you want to eat dinner...

614
00:51:37,300 --> 00:51:38,170
together tonight?

615
00:51:42,200 --> 00:51:45,480
You can go first.

616
00:51:48,480 --> 00:51:49,980
Let’s have dinner too.

617
00:51:51,750 --> 00:51:53,230
Oh, Yu.

618
00:51:54,070 --> 00:51:55,200
-Tukta.
-Yes?

619
00:51:55,200 --> 00:51:56,950
You go first. I forgot something.

620
00:51:56,950 --> 00:51:58,320
Huh? Wait!

621
00:52:00,720 --> 00:52:01,390
Yes.
